'' A GENERIC INSTANTIATION IS A TYPE NAME wherever one is allowed, and the type-argument
'' parser did not know it. 'sizeof( Box( of long ) )' was read as an EXPRESSION, so the
'' '( of long )' was dropped on the floor and only the bare name 'box' survived -- the
'' TEMPLATE, which has no size -- so the sizeof came out untyped and its statement
'' declined. Measured: fbc accepts it.
''
'' The '( of' lookahead is the same one TypeRef uses, and it consults no symbol table,
'' which this layer may not do. An UNDECLARED generic still declines, so the name is
'' doing the work rather than the shape.
''
'' The four sizes below are 4, 8, 8 and 16, and the two instantiations of Pair are
'' distinct types in the layout table.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/sizeof-instantiation.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i64 16
'' GOLDEN: expected/sizeof-instantiation.out
